        "original_id": "1fb1b5d1-105c-5e8e-a278-6665beb83c81",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Gopalpur Tussar Fabrics, shawls\n- Organizations: Government of India\n- Concepts: Geographical Indication, clothing, etymology\n\nFacts:\n- The Government of India gave Gopalpur Tussar Fabrics a Geographical Indication tag in 2009.\n- A shawl is a simple item of clothing that is loosely worn over the shoulders, upper body, and arms, and sometimes also over the head.\n- The word \"shawl\" comes from Persian and Urdu \"shāl\" and may derive from Hindi \"duśālā,\" which ultimately comes from Sanskrit \"śāṭī.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
